# THE RING BY DAY (19_orbit, src/render/orbit/): a pass staged overhead at noon,
# looked straight up at. The hull is a PALE mass -- lit from below by the sunlit
# planet and from above by the sun, the way the daytime moon is pale and never a
# hole -- asked of the live frame (`ring_pale`: lighter than the open sky beside
# it on the whole, and almost nowhere darker), and the pass moves across the sky
# while it is watched.
#   TOUR_FIXED_FPS=60 tools/tour.sh tours/orbit_sky.tour --seed=7 --place=coast --hour=12 --orbit=zenith@12 --eye=1.7,-80,70 --face=146 --weather=clear:0
wait 2
await ring 5
await ring_pale 5
shot 00-noon-ghost
wait 3
shot 01-noon-moving
wait 3
shot 02-noon-moving
